message: "If you use Arbiter MCP in your research, project, or product, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Arbiter MCP — Open-Source AI Agent for IT Ticket Triage"
abstract: >
  Arbiter MCP (4ciki/arbiter-mcp) is an open-source, provider-agnostic AI agent
  for autonomous IT helpdesk ticket triage and resolution. It combines LangGraph
  stateful orchestration, ChromaDB semantic retrieval, a deterministic three-component
  trust score (retrieval similarity + category success rate + LLM confidence), and a
  hard safety override to auto-resolve low-risk tickets and escalate high-risk ones to
  humans via Slack — with a median end-to-end latency of 1.03 seconds and a 0%
  false-positive auto-resolution rate over N=40 benchmark tickets.
  Integrates natively with Jira via the Atlassian Rovo MCP protocol and Slack via
  HMAC-SHA256 verified webhooks. Built with FastAPI, Streamlit, and SQLite. Apache 2.0.
